WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.652 --> 00:00:16.245
Mr. Chen I could use his mirror for a while longer.

2
00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:20.368
So I carried the magic box upstairs to my apartment.

3
00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:23.110
Molly came with me.

4
00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:27.213
I knew what I wanted to do next with it.

5
00:00:28.114 --> 00:00:30.176
I wanted to try to read my mother's thoughts.

6
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.521
All I had to do was persuade Mom to put her head inside the box.

7
00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:40.022
Tate was in the living room.

8
00:00:40.042 --> 00:00:41.543
"What's that?"

9
00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:43.443
he asked, looking at my box.

10
00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:46.624
"A magic thinking box," I said.

11
00:00:46.644 --> 00:00:49.405
"I'm bringing it to the Invention Convention."

12
00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:53.626
"It looks weird," said Tate.

13
00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:55.687
"What's it supposed to do?"

14
00:00:55.707 --> 00:01:00.608
"When you put it over your head, Iggy can tell what you're thinking!"

15
00:01:01.104 --> 00:01:01.785
said Molly.

16
00:01:01.805 --> 00:01:03.666
"Want to try it?"

17
00:01:03.986 --> 00:01:04.466
I asked.

18
00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:08.209
"Okay," said Tate.

19
00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:10.971
"But you'll never be able to tell what I'm thinking."

20
00:01:12.332 --> 00:01:15.554
Tate put the box over his head, and I gave him the flashlight.

21
00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:19.637
"Now turn on the flashlight," I said.

22
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:24.180
Tate turned the flashlight on inside the magic thinking box.

23
00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:27.702
I turned off the light in the room.

24
00:01:27.722 --> 00:01:31.329
"I can see you," I said.

25
00:01:31.349 --> 00:01:33.010
"But you can't see me."

26
00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.172
"Big deal," said Tate.

27
00:01:36.193 --> 00:01:38.534
"You still can't tell what I'm thinking."

28
00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:41.757
"Yes, I can," I said.

29
00:01:41.777 --> 00:01:45.180
"You're thinking this is a dumb invention."

30
00:01:46.741 --> 00:01:49.363
Tate took the box off his head with a big grin.

31
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:51.885
"Well, you got that right!"

32
00:01:52.206 --> 00:01:52.726
he said.

33
00:01:52.746 --> 00:01:55.909
"See, Iggy's invention works!"

34
00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.170
said Molly.

35
00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:01.252
"Let's try it on my mom now," I whispered to Molly.

36
00:02:02.473 --> 00:02:04.033
Molly and I went into the kitchen.

37
00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:07.014
For once Mom wasn't on the phone.

38
00:02:08.034 --> 00:02:10.715
She was baking cookies, just like a normal mother.

39
00:02:10.735 --> 00:02:13.696
"Will you try my new invention, Mom?"

40
00:02:14.036 --> 00:02:14.496
I asked.

41
00:02:15.136 --> 00:02:16.096
I showed her the box.

42
00:02:16.116 --> 00:02:18.477
"It really works, Mrs.

43
00:02:18.557 --> 00:02:20.177
Erickson!" added Molly.

44
00:02:21.378 --> 00:02:24.819
My mom slid a tray of cookies into the oven and then looked at me.

45
00:02:24.839 --> 00:02:27.179
"What do I have to do?"

46
00:02:27.199 --> 00:02:30.805
"Just put the box over your head," I said.

47
00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:34.648
"You want me to put my head in that box?"

48
00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:35.869
said Mom.

49
00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:39.112
"Just for a minute, Mom," I said.

50
00:02:39.132 --> 00:02:44.016
"Please?" "Well, okay."

51
00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.879
Mom sat down, and I put the box over her head.

52
00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:49.981
Molly laughed.

53
00:02:50.001 --> 00:02:53.364
"You look funny, Mrs.

54
00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:58.288
Erickson!" "I feel funny," said Mom.

55
00:02:59.124 --> 00:03:00.664
"It's very dark in here."

56
00:03:00.684 --> 00:03:04.926
"Here's the flashlight," I said.

57
00:03:04.946 --> 00:03:08.066
"Molly, can you please turn off the kitchen light?"

58
00:03:11.647 --> 00:03:14.548
Pretty soon Molly and I were looking through the one-way mirror.

59
00:03:14.568 --> 00:03:18.149
"All I can see is myself," said Mom.

60
00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:21.410
"We can see you," I told her.

61
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:23.471
I stared at Mom's face.

62
00:03:25.591 --> 00:03:28.112
She was frowning as she stared at herself in the glass.

63
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.102
"And I can tell what you're thinking!"

64
00:03:31.122 --> 00:03:33.984
"Really?" said Mom.

65
00:03:34.004 --> 00:03:37.548
"What?" "You're thinking about money!"

66
00:03:37.928 --> 00:03:38.308
I said.

67
00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:40.710
"About how you're going to get some!"

68
00:03:41.992 --> 00:03:43.113
Mom took off the box.

69
00:03:43.953 --> 00:03:45.295
"Your invention works, Iggy.

70
00:03:45.695 --> 00:03:49.198
I was thinking about money—about how I need a whole bank!"

71
00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:51.860
Molly and I looked at each other.

72
00:03:52.861 --> 00:03:55.464
I didn't need a magic box to read her mind this time.

73
00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:00.004
I already knew what Molly was thinking because it was exactly what I was thinking.

74
00:04:02.326 --> 00:04:06.269
What if I hadn't invented the story about Mom planning to rob a bank?

75
00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.731
What if it was true?

76
00:04:10.913 --> 00:04:14.016
Soon the cookies were done, and the kitchen was full of delicious smells.

77
00:04:16.939 --> 00:04:22.124
Josh and Jenny came up to my apartment, and we all ate the chewy chocolate cookies.

78
00:04:25.168 --> 00:04:28.992
I decided to enjoy the cookies and stop worrying about Mom for a little while.

79
00:04:29.012 --> 00:04:33.737
"Robbing a bank takes lots of planning," I told myself.

80
00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:39.002
If Mom was going to rob her bank, she couldn't do it right away.

81
00:04:39.943 --> 00:04:46.269
Plus, I needed my brain for something else besides worrying: getting ready for the Invention Convention.
